subject: [[your old clients | who's calling your old clients? | the clients in your ats]]

Hi {first_name|there},

(({company.opener}))

{first_name|This address} is listed on the {company_name} site((, as {title})).

Short version: I'll work to book you {offer.goal} meetings with past clients from your ATS in the next {offer.days} days. If I book none, you get every fee back.

Most hiring managers who ever paid you a fee haven't heard from you in a year. Some moved to new companies with new budgets. A few are hiring this month and will call whoever reached out last.

I'm William, a software engineer from the University of Waterloo. I've built production systems with big teams and small ones. At the Government of Canada, I built a policy assistant that 17,000 staff use instead of searching 220+ directives by hand. In a small University of Alberta research lab, I built a tool that cut 200+ hours of manual lookups across 7,000+ records. Now I build systems like these for recruiting firms.

Here's the plan. You send an export of past clients. I clean it, check every address, and write to them in your recruiter's name from a new domain, so your main one is never touched. You approve the emails first, and warm replies reach your recruiter the same day.

From you, that's the export and one 30-minute kickoff call. I take {offer.slots} firms at a time so I can run each one myself.

Want to see how it works first? Here is a short walkthrough: {link.watch}

William
